# Security headers for the frontend static site itself.
#
# Helmet (backend/server.js) only sets headers on the Express API's JSON
# responses — it has no effect on the React app's own HTML/JS/CSS, which is
# served separately as static files. If deploying to Netlify, this file is
# picked up automatically and applies these headers to every response.
# (If deploying elsewhere — Vercel, S3+CloudFront, nginx — configure the
# equivalent headers there instead; see vercel.json for the Vercel version.)

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), camera=(), microphone=()
  X-XSS-Protection: 0
